.azure
.venv
.pytest_cache
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.log
# `.env*`, not `.env`. Docker does not read `.gitignore`, so a file git ignores
# is still in the build context — and the bare rule this used to carry would
# have let `.env.local` or `.env.production` through. This image is not actually
# exposed by that, because the COPY lines below name their paths explicitly and
# never take the context wholesale; the pattern is widened anyway so the
# protection does not depend on nobody ever writing `COPY . .`. `apps/web`
# already carries `.env*` for the same reason, and the demo app had no
# `.dockerignore` at all until one was added — Docker resolves it from the build
# context root, so a rule here does not cover a context set to a subdirectory.
.env*
apps/web/node_modules
apps/web/dist
data/documents
